# Copy to a secure path outside Git. Set every CHANGE_ME value before startup.
APP_ENV=production
AWWO_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://CHANGE_ME_PUBLIC_HOST
# Optional public ClawHunt main-site navigation, baked into the web image.
# Empty hides the link. Rebuild web after changing this value.
VITE_CLAWHUNT_SITE_URL=
# Optional main-site identity provider. Set all three together; API only.
# Empty keeps standalone accounts. See docs/clawhunt-identity.md.
AWWO_CLAWHUNT_URL=
AWWO_CLAWHUNT_CLIENT_ID=
AWWO_CLAWHUNT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional Amazon Bedrock catalog for the operator's workers (docs/awwo-bedrock.md).
# Workers sign with the AWS credential chain the containers see unless a Bedrock API key is set.
# Bedrock is an operator destination: set AWWO_CREDENTIAL_MODE=operator (below) before enabling it,
# or both workers refuse to start.
# builtin: verified models; builtin-all once the role may use cross-region inference profiles.
# AWWO_BEDROCK_CATALOG=builtin
# AWWO_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1
# AWWO_PI_BEDROCK_MODELS=
# AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_BEDROCK_MODELS=
# AWWO_BEDROCK_API_KEY=
# With AWWO_LLMGATE_ONLY=true the API and both workers also need:
# AWWO_PLATFORM_PROVIDERS=llmgate,bedrock

# Optional defaults for workspaces created from now on; existing workspaces keep
# theirs. Unset keeps today's behaviour: every model, 100 runs a day, no cap. Models
# follow the admin allowedModels rules (comma-separated, no spaces) and need
# AWWO_CREDENTIAL_MODE=operator; user mode refuses them at startup. The cap answers
# POST /tenants with 403 workspace_limit for an account that is not a platform admin
# and owns at least that many; the workspace created at sign-up is never refused.
# API only; example:
# AWWO_NEW_WORKSPACE_ALLOWED_MODELS=qwen3.8-27b-p6
# AWWO_NEW_WORKSPACE_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY=50
# AWWO_MAX_OWNED_WORKSPACES=1

# Optional daily allowances per paid model route, inside the daily runs above
# (backend/internal/app/route_limits.go). gate = text models other than the free list,
# bedrock = bedrock.* models, media = image and video generations. New workspaces get
# AWWO_NEW_WORKSPACE_ROUTE_LIMITS; AWWO_ROUTE_TOTAL_PER_DAY caps each route across all
# route-limited workspaces but an empty {}; AWWO_ROUTE_FREE_MODELS (required with a gate limit) are the
# self-hosted models that spend only the daily runs. Operator credential mode only.
# Existing workspaces keep no route limits unless an admin sets routeLimits. API only:
# AWWO_NEW_WORKSPACE_ROUTE_LIMITS=gate=3,bedrock=1,media=1
# AWWO_ROUTE_TOTAL_PER_DAY=gate=300,bedrock=30,media=50
# AWWO_ROUTE_FREE_MODELS=qwen3.8-27b-p6,qwen3.8-27b
# Optional deployment-wide ceiling on the free list's own calls per UTC day, across the same route-limited
# workspaces (not {}); past it a run fails with free_capacity_exceeded. Paid-plan and operator planner calls
# neither count nor are held. Unset or 0: no ceiling. Needs AWWO_ROUTE_FREE_MODELS. API only:
# AWWO_FREE_MODEL_TOTAL_PER_DAY=5000
# Optional free-allowance promotion with daily check-ins (backend/internal/app/promo.go), until AWWO_PROMO_UNTIL (RFC 3339;
# every other line below needs it). Free workspaces get at least the daily calls and route allowances below, the
# deployment-wide ceilings rise to the values below, and a member may check in once a UTC day for the bonus that day.
# It only raises, writes nothing to a workspace and ends by itself. Operator credential mode only. API only:
# AWWO_PROMO_UNTIL=2026-10-29T00:00:00Z
# AWWO_PROMO_DAILY=100
# AWWO_PROMO_ROUTE_LIMITS=media=5
# AWWO_PROMO_ROUTE_TOTAL_PER_DAY=gate=600,bedrock=60
# AWWO_PROMO_MEDIA_TOTAL_RUNS_PER_DAY=400
# AWWO_PROMO_TRIPO_FREE_TOTAL_PER_DAY=100
# AWWO_CHECKIN_BONUS=daily=50,media=3
# Models only a paid plan (Pro / Max) or the operator's own workspaces (owned by a platform administrator) run; any
# other workspace sees them tagged Pro and a call on them fails with premium_quota_exceeded. Empty or unset: Claude
# Opus 5.5 (owner 2026-10-13); "none": no model. API only:
# AWWO_PLAN_ONLY_MODELS=bedrock.claude-opus-5-5

# Optional limits on the account a first ClawHunt sign-in creates (backend/internal/app/clawhunt_signup.go);
# existing accounts always sign in. Accounts per client address per UTC day (an IPv6 address by its /64), counted
# under a keyed hash, never the address; behind a proxy set AWWO_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS first, or every visitor shares
# the proxy's count. Unset or 0: no limit. Verified email: no account for an identity ClawHunt reports unverified.
# Both need ClawHunt sign-in. API only:
# AWWO_NEW_ACCOUNTS_PER_IP_PER_DAY=3
# AWWO_REQUIRE_VERIFIED_EMAIL=true

# Optional operator-paid model for canvas plans (backend/internal/app/planner_model.go), e.g. a Claude model
# on Bedrock that the Pi worker serves. Only plans the canvas assistant requests use it, outside the workspace's
# allowlist, route allowances and plan credits; they still count towards its daily runs. Over a ceiling, over
# the input bound or when the worker lacks the model, the plan runs on the default model. Ceilings are calls per
# UTC day (0: none). Empty model: off. Operator credential mode only. API only:
# AWWO_PLANNER_MODEL=bedrock.claude-haiku-4-5
# AWWO_PLANNER_PER_WORKSPACE_PER_DAY=20
# AWWO_PLANNER_TOTAL_PER_DAY=2000
# AWWO_PLANNER_MAX_INPUT_BYTES=60000
# The Pi worker may let only that model think (AWWO_PI_BEDROCK_THINKING_BUDGET, 1024-16000 tokens, with
# AWWO_PI_BEDROCK_THINKING_MODELS naming it); empty: no thinking.
# AWWO_PI_BEDROCK_THINKING_BUDGET=2048
# AWWO_PI_BEDROCK_THINKING_MODELS=bedrock.claude-haiku-4-5

# Paid plans (backend/internal/app/plans.go, billing.go, plan_sync.go): Pro $20 / Max $100 a month, sold and
# renewed by ClawHunt (Stripe) and read over the SSO backchannel. A route-limited workspace whose owner has a plan
# spends the owner's credits for the paid period (what was paid, 1 credit = 1 cent; official price x 1.5 from
# AWWO_MODEL_PRICING_JSON below, which must price every paid model a plan may call: an unpriced one is refused;
# a call whose usage is never reported is estimated from its size, never less than a large call) on the routes
# above instead of their limits. Checkout stays closed until this is true, and true needs ClawHunt sign-in,
# AWWO_ROUTE_FREE_MODELS, AWWO_NEW_WORKSPACE_ROUTE_LIMITS (plans apply to route-limited workspaces only) and
# AWWO_MODEL_PRICING_JSON; plans already bought keep working either way. API only:
# AWWO_BILLING_CHECKOUT_ENABLED=false

# Optional image and video nodes through RunningHub (docs/awwo-runninghub.md). API only.
# Needs an Enterprise-Shared key; generated files are kept on the media-data volume, which
# belongs in your backups. Workspaces with a model allowlist must also allow the rh.* models.
# The key and AWWO_MEDIA_DIR are required together: compose.yml sets AWWO_MEDIA_DIR to the
# media-data volume when the key is set; other deployments must set it to a persistent,
# writable absolute directory.
# AWWO_RUNNINGHUB_API_KEY=
# AWWO_RUNNINGHUB_BASE_URL=https://www.runninghub.ai
# Image and video nodes through X-tasy (the operator's own platform, service.xtasyart.com). Needs AWWO_MEDIA_DIR like
# RunningHub; with both keys set the X-tasy models are listed first. Keep the key out of the repository.
# AWWO_XTASY_API_KEY=
# AWWO_XTASY_BASE_URL=https://service.xtasyart.com
# Offer the X-tasy models to every workspace whatever its model allowlist (needs AWWO_MAX_OWNED_WORKSPACES).
# AWWO_XTASY_ALL_WORKSPACES=false
# Image and video nodes on the operator's Jimeng member account, through Jimeng's official canvas CLI (dreamina-canvas).
# Install it on the host, sign it in once as the API's user with
#   HOME=<AWWO_JIMENG_HOME> dreamina-canvas --profile <AWWO_JIMENG_PROFILE> --non-interactive auth login
# and approve the printed link in a browser (then `auth wait --device-code <code>`). Needs AWWO_MEDIA_DIR; both
# directories below must be outside it, owned by the API's user, mode 0700. The sign-in never goes in this file.
# AWWO_JIMENG_CLI=/srv/awwo/bin/dreamina-canvas
# AWWO_JIMENG_HOME=/srv/awwo/saas-staging/jimeng
# AWWO_JIMENG_PROFILE=awwo
# AWWO_JIMENG_STATE_DIR=/srv/awwo/saas-staging/jimeng/state
# Most Jimeng credits one generation may spend; a quote above it stops before anything is made.
# AWWO_JIMENG_CREDIT_CEILING=700
# Jimeng spends a personal member account, so its models are offered only explicitly: these workspace ids
# (comma-separated), every workspace (needs AWWO_MAX_OWNED_WORKSPACES), or a workspace allowlist naming them.
# AWWO_JIMENG_WORKSPACES=
# AWWO_JIMENG_ALL_WORKSPACES=false
# AWWO_MEDIA_TIMEOUT=20m
# AWWO_MEDIA_RUNS_PER_DAY=30
# Ceiling across all workspaces each UTC day, a backstop on the operator's spend.
# AWWO_MEDIA_TOTAL_RUNS_PER_DAY=500
# AWWO_MEDIA_MAX_FILE_MB=300
# No generation is admitted, and no result written, below this much free space.
# AWWO_MEDIA_MIN_FREE_MB=2048
# Generations are paid from this key, so a workspace may use a media model only when its
# model allowlist names it, unless this opts workspaces without an allowlist in.
# Opening media to every unrestricted or new workspace also requires AWWO_MAX_OWNED_WORKSPACES.
# AWWO_MEDIA_UNRESTRICTED_WORKSPACES=false
AWWO_INGRESS_PORT=8189
AWWO_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_DATABASE_PASSWORD
# URL-encode the password. Use TLS for external/managed PostgreSQL.
AWWO_DATABASE_URL=postgres://awwo:CHANGE_ME_DATABASE_PASSWORD@database:5432/awwo?sslmode=disable
AWWO_PI_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME_RANDOM_INTERNAL_TOKEN_AT_LEAST_32_CHARS
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME_DIFFERENT_RANDOM_INTERNAL_TOKEN_AT_LEAST_32_CHARS
AWWO_OPENMAUS_TOKEN=CHANGE_ME_ANOTHER_RANDOM_INTERNAL_TOKEN_AT_LEAST_32_CHARS
# Operator workspace settings only; end users continue using My engines.
# Build deploy/saas/workspace once on this daemon and use its immutable digest.
AWWO_OPENMAUS_WORKSPACE_IMAGE=awwo-workspace:20261016
AWWO_OPENMAUS_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
AWWO_WORKSPACE_DOCKER_SOCKET=/var/run/docker.sock
AWWO_WORKSPACE_DOCKER_GID=999
AWWO_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=CHANGE_ME_ADMIN_EMAIL
AWWO_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_ADMIN_PASSWORD

# All API/workers must agree. Users supply personal provider keys after login.
AWWO_CREDENTIAL_MODE=user
# Generate once: openssl rand -base64 32
# Keep this stable and backed up with your database. Never commit it.
AWWO_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY=CHANGE_ME_BASE64_32_BYTE_KEY

# Optional Jev sponsor budget, separate from BYOK model execution. These must be
# passed only to the API service, never workers or the browser. Default off.
# Enabling requires an exact workspace allowlist; wildcard entries are rejected.
AWWO_TYPESAFE_SPONSORED_PLANNING=false
AWWO_TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
AWWO_TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-1.13.0
AWWO_TYPESAFE_ENABLED_TENANT_IDS=
AWWO_TYPESAFE_TIMEOUT=10s
AWWO_TYPESAFE_MAX_EVALUATIONS_PER_DAY=20

# Legacy external executor API only; the default UI uses managed execution above. Each OpenMaus origin must serve
# exactly one tenant. Use a paired token and an HTTPS origin reachable from the
# API container. Never expose this JSON to browser or worker environments.
# Example structure: [{"tenantId":"...","url":"https://maus.example.com","token":"..."}]
AWWO_OPENMAUS_CONNECTIONS_JSON=[]

# Optional password recovery. Register/login work without SMTP; recovery reports
# unavailability until this is configured. Sender must be verified by your provider.
AWWO_SMTP_HOST=
AWWO_SMTP_PORT=587
AWWO_SMTP_FROM=
AWWO_SMTP_USERNAME=
AWWO_SMTP_PASSWORD=

AWWO_PI_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# Legacy operator-mode capacities. Personal connections use the conservative
# envelope documented in docs/personal-accounts.md instead of shared profiles.
AWWO_PI_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
AWWO_PI_MAX_TOKENS=16384
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_MAX_TOKENS=16384
AWWO_PI_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
AWWO_RUN_TIMEOUT=600s
# Per-download retained run archive limit (1 MiB to 256 MiB).
AWWO_RUN_ARCHIVE_MAX_BYTES=16777216
# How many times a canvas node runs again by itself after its run failed for a transient reason (a worker or
# provider that was unavailable, busy or rate limited, a dropped stream, a run timeout), 0 to 5; 0 turns automatic
# retries off. Each attempt is a run of its own, admitted and counted like any other; the first waits 15 s, each
# later one twice as long, at most 120 s. Anything else is refused at startup.
AWWO_GRAPH_NODE_RETRIES=2
AWWO_PI_SESSION_WAIT=5s
AWWO_OPENAI_AGENTS_TOOLS_JSON=[]

# Exact ingress IPs/CIDRs only. Empty ignores forwarded headers.
AWWO_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=
AWWO_METRICS_ENABLED=false
AWWO_OTEL_ENABLED=false
AWWO_REVISION=unknown
AWWO_MODEL_PRICING_JSON=
AWWO_USAGE_RETENTION_DAYS=180

# Legacy operator mode is opt-in and documented in docs/personal-accounts.md.
# Shared execution provider keys remain excluded from personal-mode deployments.
